what Gauge's own setting table names ledger rows, witness headers, scan comments and commit bodies as Meter, uncapped on register, grade and cross-references. The report card forces every program head to Door -- grade ceiling 9, one cross-reference per hundred words, register against 20 percent -- and drops a typed --setting meter on a program in silence. Refusal prose that names its own paths is exactly what a witness header is, so the population reads below B for writing the way the law tells it to. Add a genre reading that names witness, scan, control or module from the basename, publish a meter shadow composite beside the Door grade the way reach_shadow and ordered_list already do, and make the dropped flag say so out loud. Reported, never scored -- admitting it would re-grade the tree in one unmeasured step, and the cost belongs on the card as a question for Keaton.
claim incense-booked-red-is-claimable
seat incense
