paths tools/f/fleet_baton.txt .claude/rules/the-baton.md .cursor/rules/the-baton.mdc construction/REDS.md
what The claim clause asks a lap to say-before-you-build only when it opens a NEW INSTRUMENT, and a repair is exempt because it collides with nothing. That reasoning holds for an ordinary repair and fails for a booked red: a row standing OPEN on a shared pin is a published invitation every one of eight ships can read at once, which is the loudest collision signal the fleet emits and the one thing the clause excuses. It cost incense a whole build on 20260916 -- %782's repair, run through the claim check, claimed by nobody, landed by grass forty minutes ahead and strictly better. Measured over 131 claim openings: 53 named only paths that already existed, so the fleet already claims repairs 53 times under a clause that never asked, and 18 name a REDS row outright. Fifteen rows stand OPEN or BOOKED on the pin now. Widen the clause on the baton, its law page and the Cursor twin so a claim covers a new instrument OR a booked red, keeping the ordinary repair exempt.
